# steps/named-struct-exec.md §11, slice 4 (REVIEW dd07174; fable_pc's M36 and probe ns4_two_types): two
# executed fields of two types -- `Other: o` then `Model: m` -- each runs its own type's code: m\v = 2,
# o\w = 15.  With the type dropped (every field takes the first Structure's code), o runs Model's code
# over its data and o\w reads 2.  Entry 7.
Model:
    size_t: v 1U
    v: v + 1U
return
Other:
    size_t: w 10U
    w: w + 5U
return
Model: m
Other: o
o
m
size_t: a 0U
a: m\v
size_t: b 0U
b: o\w
int: ok 0
if: a = 2U && b = 15U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
